{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Module Homomorphism.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Module Homomorphism.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"module homomorphism module homomorphism","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Module Homomorphism.md","fileName":"Module Homomorphism.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Module Homomorphism","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Module Structure and Exact Sequences]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Module Structure and Exact Sequences","Submodule","Exact Sequence","Hom Module","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Module Homomorphism.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Module Homomorphism.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"module homomorphism module homomorphism","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Module Homomorphism.md","fileName":"Module Homomorphism.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Module Homomorphism","heading":"Module Homomorphism","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A module homomorphism is a map f: M → N that preserves addition and scalar multiplication. It sends a linear combination r₁m₁ + r₂m₂ to r₁f(m₁) + r₂f(m₂).\n\nKernels and images of module homomorphisms are [[Submodule]]s. Families of these maps form [[Exact Sequence]]s, and all maps from M to N together form the [[Hom Module]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Module Structure and Exact Sequences","Submodule","Exact Sequence","Hom Module","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Module Homomorphism.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Module Homomorphism.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"module homomorphism module homomorphism","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Module Homomorphism.md","fileName":"Mod